course: dictionary
lesson: 9942
title: Tarmac: a word with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things you see every day, and tarmac is one of them. «A road is built in layers: crushed stone rolled hard at the bottom, then hot asphalt, a mix of stones and sticky black bitumen, spread and rolled flat on top; people often call it tarmac.» The clues are crushed stone, sticky black and rolled flat, and they all describe the surface of a road.
explain: Tarmac can also mean the area of an airport where planes park and take off. To choose the right meaning, read the words around it. Is the sentence about a road or about a plane? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Tarmac is an uncountable noun, so we talk about some tarmac, or the tarmac when we mean a particular place. Notice that the word is used for a material in one sentence and for a place in another.
fact: Tarmac is a noun, which is the name of a thing.
fact: Tarmac is a hard black material for roads and paths, made of crushed stones mixed with tar.
fact: «The tarmac» often means the area of an airport where planes park and take off.
fact: On a hot day, dark tarmac can get very hot and even soft, and dark surfaces take in more heat from the sun than light ones.
fact: Check the meaning by swapping your idea into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
exercise: What is tarmac made of? | Sand and water | Glass and paper | *Crushed stones mixed with tar | Wood and glue
exercise: A plane waits on «the tarmac» at the airport. Where is the plane? | A school playground | *The area of an airport where planes park | A forest | A river bank
exercise: Find and copy one word from «A road is built in layers: crushed stone rolled hard at the bottom, then hot asphalt, a mix of stones and sticky black bitumen, spread and rolled flat on top» that describes the colour of the top layer. | *black | crushed | bottom | layers
test: Why does dark tarmac get hotter than light ground on a sunny day? | Because it is made of wood | Because it is cold underneath | Because it is always wet | *Because dark surfaces take in more heat from the sun
test: Which sentence uses tarmac to mean the airport area? | «We picked apples in the orchard.» | «The cat slept on the sofa.» | «The river flowed past the old mill.» | *«The plane waited on the tarmac.»
exam: Tarmac has two meanings. Which two are correct? | *A road surface, and an airport area where planes park | Sand and water | Wood and glass | Snow and ice
